# Decimal literal above the maximum precision

Verifies a decimal literal beyond the 28-digit precision limit is rejected
with a compile-time diagnostic through the complete CLI pipeline.

>>> source
too_large: decimal = 1e100
print(too_large)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: invalid literal `1e100` for type `decimal`: Scale exceeds the maximum precision allowed: 100 > 28 at Span { start: 21, end: 26 }

<<< exit
1
